# NOTICE — source-data attribution

Urban Digital Twin is proprietary; see `LICENSE`. **This file is about the data
the project does NOT own.**

Every entry below is DERIVED FROM `src/data/source-registry.ts`, which is the
live authority for source identity, attribution strings, terms URLs and licence
class. This file quotes that registry; it does not restate it from memory. A
committed test (`scripts/source-attribution-notice.test.mjs`) asserts that every
attribution string in the registry appears here verbatim, so the two cannot
drift apart silently.

If this file and the registry ever disagree, **the registry governs.**

Obligations that travel with the data — attribution, the City of New York
modified-data disclaimer, source IDs, capture and update dates, checksums, CRS
and height uncertainty — are preserved through ingestion and presentation, and
are surfaced in the application's details panel rather than only recorded here.

## Share-alike obligations, stated plainly

Two licence classes below are SHARE-ALIKE and are **not** displaced by the
proprietary grant in `LICENSE`:

- **ODbL 1.0** — the OpenStreetMap-derived block-835 commercial frontage
  partition is retained as a declared derivative database, with attribution and
  database-offer metadata.
- **CC BY-SA 4.0** — the Wikimedia Commons photographic references used as
  cited style inputs.

## The 2026-08-11 authorization (NYC OTI Building Footprints, jh45-qr5r)

Recorded against `nyc.building-footprints` in the registry: exterior geometry
GENERATED from these footprints may be publicly displayed, conveyed as a
derivative and redistributed, provided NYC OTI attribution, the City
modified-data disclaimer, source IDs, capture timestamp, checksum, CRS and
height uncertainty travel with it. That permission covers the generated geometry
ONLY — never the raw jh45-qr5r source dataset — and public deployment remains
excluded.

